<title>INDIA: India's Ranbaxy 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India's Ranbaxy 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    1,542   vs   1,350</p>
<p>    Sales		  10,661   vs   8,713</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	 8.0   vs     5.5</p>
<p>    EPS (in rupees)	31.20  vs    30.43</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  292.0   vs   244.0</p>
<p>    Provision for tax   220.0   vs   235.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Ranbaxy Laboratories Ltd, the country's largest pharmaceutical company, said in a statement that its growth was driven by all dimensions of its business, both at home and overseas.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
